      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Under aerobic conditions, Dy(NO3)3·5H2O (0.175 g, 0.40 mmol) and Cu(ClO4)2·6H2O (0.185 g, 0.50 mmol) were added to a stirred yellowish solution of H2pdm (0.056 g, 0.40 mmol), ButCH2CO2H (25 μL, 0.20 mmol) and Et3N (252 μL, 1.80 mmol) in MeCN (5 mL)/MeOH (10 mL). The resulting blue solution was stirred for a further 30 min and stored at −16 °C. X-ray quality blue crystals of 1·4MeCN·1.5MeOH formed in 2 d, were collected by filtration, washed with cold MeCN (1 mL) and Et2O (3 × 2 mL), and dried in a vacuum desiccator over anhydrous CaCl2. The same product was also obtained using CuCl2·2H2O (0.085 g, 0.50 mmol) or Cu(NO3)2·3H2O (0.121 g, 0.50 mmol) in place of Cu(ClO4)2·6H2O.",
